---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const pageTitle = '48-Hour California Getaways';
const pageDescription =
  'Practical two-day California itineraries designed to help you make the most of a short getaway.';
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section>
    <p>48-Hour California Getaways</p>

    <h1>Two days can take you farther than you think.</h1>

    <p>
      California is made for short escapes. Our 48-hour itineraries help you
      decide where to stay, what to see, where to eat, and how to spend your
      limited time without turning a weekend getaway into a planning project.
    </p>

    <h2>Start planning your next California getaway</h2>

    <p>
      From wine country and the coast to mountain towns, desert escapes, and
      California cities, each itinerary is built around one simple idea:
      arrive with a plan and enjoy the next 48 hours.
    </p>

    <h2>Featured 48-Hour Getaways</h2>

    <h3>48 Hours in Paso Robles</h3>
    <p>
      Wine country, downtown dining, scenic drives, and enough breathing room
      to enjoy the weekend without turning it into a checklist.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/paso-robles/">Explore 48 Hours in Paso Robles</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Cambria</h3>
    <p>
      Ocean views, village wandering, coastal trails, local wine, and enough
      unscheduled time to actually enjoy being away.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/cambria/">Explore 48 Hours in Cambria</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Morro Bay</h3>
    <p>
      Harbor views, fresh seafood, coastal wildlife, and time to slow down
      beside one of California's most recognizable coastal landmarks.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/morro-bay/">Explore 48 Hours in Morro Bay</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Avila Beach</h3>
    <p>
      A relaxed Central Coast escape with a walkable beachfront, ocean views,
      Port San Luis, and time to enjoy the coast without overplanning the trip.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/avila-beach/">Explore 48 Hours in Avila Beach</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in San Luis Obispo</h3>
    <p>
      A lively downtown, California history, nearby wine country, and an easy
      Central Coast pace built around one of California's most enjoyable small
      cities.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/san-luis-obispo/">Explore 48 Hours in San Luis Obispo</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Monterey</h3>
    <p>
      Monterey Bay, California history, Cannery Row, coastal scenery, and time
      to experience one of the state's most distinctive seaside destinations.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/monterey/">Explore 48 Hours in Monterey</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Carmel-by-the-Sea</h3>
    <p>
      A walkable village, storybook architecture, Carmel Beach, California
      history, and some of the most memorable coastline on the Monterey
      Peninsula.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/carmel/">Explore 48 Hours in Carmel-by-the-Sea</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Big Sur</h3>
    <p>
      Dramatic coastline, redwoods, Highway 1, and enough unhurried time to
      experience Big Sur as a landscape rather than a list of stops.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/big-sur/">Explore 48 Hours in Big Sur</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Santa Barbara</h3>
    <p>
      Spanish-influenced architecture, beaches, a walkable downtown, good
      food, and a California coastal weekend with plenty of room to slow down.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/santa-barbara/">Explore 48 Hours in Santa Barbara</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Santa Ynez Valley</h3>
    <p>
      Six small communities, ranch country, vineyards, country roads, and a
      relaxed Central Coast wine-country weekend.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/santa-ynez-valley/">Explore 48 Hours in Santa Ynez Valley</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Santa Cruz</h3>
    <p>
      Redwoods, surf culture, the historic Beach Boardwalk, Monterey Bay, and
      a California coastal getaway that leaves room to enjoy where you are.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/santa-cruz/">Explore 48 Hours in Santa Cruz</a>
    </p>

    <h3>48 Hours in Sonoma</h3>
    <p>
      California history, a walkable town square, vineyard roads, good food,
      Glen Ellen, and wine country with enough breathing room to enjoy it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/itineraries/sonoma/">Explore 48 Hours in Sonoma</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
